.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_hybrid_config" "fuzzygene_hybrid_config"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_hybrid_config \- Chainable mutator of the solver and hybrid layer options.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_hybrid_config(\fBconfig\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneConfig, 
\fBsolver\fR as string = "newton", 
\fBmaxNewtonIterations\fR as integer = 20, 
\fBandersonDepth\fR as integer = 5, 
\fBcalibration\fR as string = "none", 
\fBcalibrationEpsilon\fR as double = 0.05, 
\fBcalibrationMinScale\fR as double = 0.05, 
\fBclampInputToSupport\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBclampOutputToSupport\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBmaxRegulatorCollinearity\fR as double = 1, 
\fBpbnRegularization\fR as string = "none", 
\fBpbnMinCod\fR as double = 0.05, 
\fBpbnWeight\fR as double = 1, 
\fBpbnMaxParents\fR as integer = 2, 
\fBpbnMaxGenes\fR as integer = 2000, 
\fBpbnCandidateSize\fR as integer = 5, 
\fBensembleSamples\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBmodeBiasWeight\fR as double = 0, 
\fBfcmWarmStart\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBfcmModules\fR as integer = 48, 
\fBfcmAlpha\fR as double = 1, 
\fBfcmMaxSteps\fR as integer = 200, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Chainable mutator of the solver and hybrid layer options.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBconfig\fB \fR\- the configuration created by \fBfuzzygene_config\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsolver\fB \fR\- 
 \fBnewton\fR (default), \fBanderson\fR, \fBlegacy\fR (the old damped iteration) or \fBadvance\fR
 (lagged/time series only: plain time stepping, no steady state claim)
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcalibration\fB \fR\- 
 \fBnone\fR (default), \fBspectral\fR (scale the cyclic part until the spectral radius of the
 assembled Jacobian is below \fB1 - epsilon\fR) or \fBrow-l1\fR (the conservative row norm bound)
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcalibrationEpsilon\fB \fR\- target margin \fB1 - epsilon\fR of the spectral radius. Default 0.05.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcalibrationMinScale\fB \fR\- lower bound of one calibration pass, keeps the model from collapsing. Default 0.05.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBclampInputToSupport\fB \fR\- 
 clamp the antecedent inputs to the training domain of each regulator. Turning this off
 re-enables the unbounded extrapolation of the outermost rules. Default TRUE.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBclampOutputToSupport\fB \fR\- clamp the predicted expression to the training support. Default TRUE.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmaxRegulatorCollinearity\fB \fR\- 
 upper bound of the pairwise |Pearson| between the selected regulators; 1 disables the
 constraint (default). Lowering it to 0.95 improves the conditioning of the least squares
 step at the price of selecting fewer data driven regulators.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpbnRegularization\fB \fR\- 
 \fBnone\fR (default), \fBfilter\fR (drop correlation candidates whose CoD is too low) or
 \fBweighted\fR (order the candidates by CoD). Enabling it also makes
 \fBfuzzygene_ensemble\fR available.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpbnMinCod\fB \fR\- minimum CoD for a candidate parent set. Default 0.05.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpbnWeight\fB \fR\- weight of the CoD term when \fBpbnRegularization = "weighted"\fR. Default 1.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpbnMaxParents\fB \fR\- maximum parents enumerated per target gene. Default 2.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpbnMaxGenes\fB \fR\- gene limit of the qualitative layer; above it the PBN layer is skipped. Default 2000.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpbnCandidateSize\fB \fR\- candidate pool size per target gene (prior TFs plus the top correlated genes). Default 5.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBensembleSamples\fB \fR\- 
 default sample count of \fBfuzzygene_ensemble\fR: how many times the PBN rules are resampled.
 0 (default) keeps the deterministic single solve.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmodeBiasWeight\fB \fR\- 
 how strongly a sampled boolean mode pulls the continuous solve; 0 (default) only reports
 the boolean consistency without changing the numerical result.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfcmWarmStart\fB \fR\- 
 enable the module level fuzzy cognitive map: it provides a bounded warm start for the
 per gene root finding and a surrogate answer when the solver detects a limit cycle.
 Default FALSE.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfcmModules\fB \fR\- number of modules of the coarse grained layer. Default 48.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfcmAlpha\fB \fR\- slope of the sigmoid activation. Default 1.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfcmMaxSteps\fB \fR\- propagation budget of the module layer. Default 200.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the same configuration object, so the call can be chained
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The existing \fBfuzzygene_config\fR already carries 30 optional arguments; adding the
 solver / PBN / FCM knobs there would make it unusable and would break every script that
 relies on positional arguments. This function mutates a configuration object in place
 instead, so the whole thing stays readable:
 


 
\fB
 let opts = FuzzyGene::fuzzygene_config(maxRegulators = 6, mfCount = 3);
 opts = FuzzyGene::fuzzygene_hybrid_config(opts,
     solver = "newton", pbnRegularization = "weighted", ensembleSamples = 16);
 
\fR`

 


 Defaults are chosen so that calling this function with only \fBconfig\fR changes nothing
 important: the Newton root finder is already the default solver, and the stability
 calibration stays off (the root finder does not need a contractive map, while calibrating
 a strongly cyclic fit can drop R2 from 0.86 to 0.014 — that has to be an explicit choice).
.PP
